    content: "Winter storms in Central Texas can hit hard \u2014 and when they do, falling trees and broken limbs can cause serious damage to homes, vehicles, and power lines. Whether you live in Austin, Georgetown, or anywhere across Central Texas, knowing what to do before and after a storm can protect your property and keep your family safe.\nAt Brents Tree Service, we specialize in emergency tree removal and storm cleanup, helping homeowners recover quickly and safely after ice, wind, or rain damage.\nWhat to Do If a Tree Falls on Your Property\n\n Stay Safe and Keep Your Distance If a tree or large branch has fallen, avoid going near it \u2014 especially if it\u2019s touching your roof, fence, or vehicle. Structural damage can make the area unstable, and hidden tension in the branches can cause sudden movement.\n Check for Power Line Contact If the tree has fallen on or near power lines, do not approach or attempt removal. Contact your utility company immediately. Even downed lines that look harmless may still be live.\n Document the Damage for Insurance Take clear photos and videos from a safe distance. Most insurance companies require this before tree removal begins.\n Call a Professional Emergency Tree Service Contact Brents Tree Service right away for 24/7 emergency response. Our experienced crew uses specialized equipment to safely remove fallen trees and clear debris without causing further damage to your property.\n\nWhy You Should Avoid DIY Tree Removal\nIt can be tempting to grab a chainsaw and handle cleanup yourself \u2014 but storm-damaged trees are unpredictable and dangerous. Here\u2019s why you should leave it to professionals:\n\n Hidden tension in cracked or twisted branches can cause them to snap unexpectedly.\n Electrical hazards from nearby power lines can result in severe injury.\n Heavy equipment and climbing gear are often needed to safely remove large trees.\n\nAt Brents Tree Service, we\u2019re trained to handle these complex situations safely and efficiently, minimizing risk to both you and your property.\nHow Brents Tree Service Helps After a Storm\nWhen winter weather strikes, we\u2019re ready. Our emergency tree removal team provides fast, reliable help throughout Austin, Georgetown, and surrounding Central Texas communities.\nHere\u2019s what you can expect:\n\n 24/7 emergency response \u2014 day or night\n Safe removal of fallen or hazardous trees\n Cleanup and hauling of debris\n Damage assessment and recommendations for next steps\n\nWe also offer preventative tree trimming and inspection services to reduce storm risk before severe weather hits.\nPrevent Storm Damage Before It Happens\nThe best way to avoid emergency tree removal is through regular maintenance. Schedule an inspection before winter \u2014 our certified arborists can identify weak limbs, diseased trees, or structural issues that make your property more vulnerable during storms.\nCall Brents Tree Service for Emergency Tree Removal in Central Texas\nWhen storms strike, don\u2019t face it alone. Brents Tree Service is here to help you restore safety and peace of mind fast.\nCall us 24/7 for emergency tree removal in Austin, Georgetown, and surrounding areas. Fast response | Licensed & insured | Trusted local experts\nLet our team handle the heavy lifting \u2014 so you can focus on what matters most: keeping your family safe.",
